INT. CITY LIBRARY - CARD CATALOG ROOM - DAY

Oak cabinets floor to ceiling, brass pulls, a ladder on rails. Dust and quiet.

CLERK PHINEAS (60s, sleeve garters, wire spectacles) slides a drawer shut and opens another without looking, while DR. SOLANGE (40s, tweed, a notebook open on her forearm) climbs the ladder, taps a drawer, and mutters a number, and YUSUF (20s, backpack, earbuds hanging) crouches by a low cabinet, flipping cards with one finger and reading each aloud under his breath.

PHINEAS
It would be under P, Doctor. P for Pemberton.

SOLANGE
(from the ladder)
It was under W the last time.

YUSUF
Wait, which one are we looking for?

PHINEAS
Pemberton's Almanac of Local Murders.

SOLANGE
Whitcombe's Almanac, Phineas.

PHINEAS
Whitcombe wrote nothing of the sort.

YUSUF
There's a Whitcombe here. Whitcombe, Edmund. "Almanac of Unsolved Disappearances."

SOLANGE
That's the one.

PHINEAS
That is not Pemberton.

SOLANGE
I never said Pemberton.

YUSUF
You did. Twice.

SOLANGE
Yusuf, don't.

YUSUF
I'm just saying.

Phineas closes his drawer, folds his hands, and studies the two of them. Yusuf grins at the card.

YUSUF (CONT'D)
Call number nine-four-one. Basement stacks.

PHINEAS
Of course it is.

SOLANGE
Lead on.
